926.2	gate: a delta-only classification is reported as pending, not as stale	a pending entry is a not-shipped id an open change's delta spec introduces, so the intersection is the set that reports one; the remainder is the stale state and counting it as pending is the conflation issue #926 removed
926.3	gate: a delta-only classification is not a stale entry	a stale entry is a not-shipped id no open change introduces — the remainder — so the intersection is the pending state, and reporting a capability on its way as one that has left is the defect this split exists for
926.4	gate: a delta-only classification is reported as pending, not as stale	the pending figure counts the pending set, so reading it from the stale one prints the wrong state's number while both sets stay correct — one regression the direct assertions on the two figures cannot see
926.5	gate: a delta-only classification is not a stale entry	the stale figure counts the stale set, so reading it from the pending one prints a capability on its way as one that has left, which is exactly the reading issue #926 was filed against
